From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 03:13:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: learn the swap_pace floor with
 swap_pace on

The swap_pace floor was learned only while swap_pace was off, since a
held swap overstates it. With swap_pace on by default it was then never
learned on the J604 and the 1.75 ms fallback stayed in use, about six
times the floor measured from the same point (193 to 344 us), which held
some swaps too early.

Learn from every swap that was not held, and lower the fallback used
before the first estimate to 350 us.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit ea5c4a2a40b39985d864f95e452cb664ac85b90a)
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index e7c9149ef1..0a71e1fb2e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -1122,6 +1122,8 @@ struct dcp_m4_runtime {
 	 * full window of DCP_M4_PACE_WINDOW swaps, and the current window).
 	 */
 	u64 int_start_cnt;
+	/* The swap in flight was held by swap_pace (its start time overstates the floor). */
+	bool int_held;
 	u64 int_lat_min;
 	u64 int_lat_win;
 	u32 int_lat_n;
@@ -1786,12 +1788,12 @@ static void dcp_m4_pace_learn(struct dcp_m4_runtime *r)
 		return;
 	WRITE_ONCE(r->int_start_cnt, 0);
 	/*
-	 * A paced swap starts on purpose well before the tick it aims at, so
+	 * A held swap starts on purpose well before the tick it aims at, so
 	 * its start-to-completion time overstates the floor, and a window of
 	 * them would raise the estimate by up to a tick each time. Learn from
-	 * unpaced swaps only; the estimate stands while swap_pace is on.
+	 * swaps that were not held only.
 	 */
-	if (READ_ONCE(swap_pace))
+	if (r->int_held)
 		return;
 	lat = done - start;
 	if (!r->int_lat_n || lat < r->int_lat_win)
@@ -2708,7 +2710,7 @@ static unsigned long dcp_m4_swap_pace_us(struct dcp_m4_runtime *r)
 	if (lead_us)
 		lead = div_u64(freq * lead_us, USEC_PER_SEC);
 	else
-		lead = READ_ONCE(r->int_lat_min) ?: div_u64(freq * 7, 4000);
+		lead = READ_ONCE(r->int_lat_min) ?: div_u64(freq * 7, 20000);
 	/* The first grid tick base + k * half (k even) at least lead + margin ahead. */
 	k = div64_u64(now + lead + margin - base + half - 1, half);
 	k += k & 1;
@@ -2809,6 +2811,7 @@ static int dcp_m4_runtime_swap_full(struct dcp_m4_runtime *r, bool primary,
 
 		if (pace)
 			usleep_range(pace, pace + 50);
+		r->int_held = pace != 0;
 		WRITE_ONCE(r->int_start_cnt, __arch_counter_get_cntpct());
 		if (pace && r->pace_start && r->int_start_cnt > r->pace_start) {
 			u64 over = r->int_start_cnt - r->pace_start;
-- 
